// Monster vocabulary: every monster kind, declared as an ordered entry
// list. The kind is the monster's identity — there is no separate
// race, class, or individual id. Each entry carries the kind's speed
// (an index into the speed rate table); this table is where monster
// gameplay data (hit dice, armor, blows) grows. Load assigns each id a
// runtime handle in entry order; handles are unstable across loads
// (entry order decides them), so saved data must translate through the
// id mapping, never store raw handles.
[ ( monster: "giant_white_rat", speed: 110 ) ]
